# Crate Structure Rules

## Workspace Layout

```toml
# Cargo.toml (root)
[workspace]
members = [
    "crates/engine_core",
    "crates/script_editor",
    "crates/game_player",
]
resolver = "2"

[workspace.dependencies]
# Manage shared dependencies at workspace level
serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
rmp-serde = "1"
anyhow = "1"
thiserror = "2"
log = "0.4"
```

## Crate Overview

### `engine_core` - Core (Model)

- **Responsibility**: Core game engine logic.
- **Submodules**:
  - `ecs/` - Entity Component System foundation
  - `renderer/` - Filament wrappers and multi-view rendering
  - `live2d/` - Live2D Cubism SDK FFI wrappers
  - `vrm/` - VRM/FBX loader and SpringBone
  - `audio/` - kira/rodio-based sound system
  - `asset/` - Async asset loader and cache
  - `script/` - Tag-based script parser and state machine
  - `scene/` - Scene trait and scene manager
  - `input/` - Input abstraction
  - `save/` - Save/load (MessagePack)
  - `rng/` - Dual RNG (Xoshiro256++ / ChaCha8)
  - `ffi/` - Isolated C/C++ FFI boundary modules

### `script_editor` - Authoring Tool

- **Responsibility**: Script editing, live preview, visual editing.
- **Dependency**: Depends on `engine_core`.
- **Submodules**:
  - `ui/` - Editor UI (MVVM + Signal)
  - `preview/` - Live preview engine
  - `inspector/` - Live2D parameter and 3D placement editing
  - `project/` - Project management and asset browser

### `game_player` - Distribution Runtime

- **Responsibility**: Lightweight runtime without editor/debug features.
- **Dependency**: Depends on `engine_core`.
- **Submodules**:
  - `archive/` - Asset archive handling
  - `runtime/` - Main loop and configuration loading

## Dependency Rules

```text
game_player ──→ engine_core
script_editor ──→ engine_core
```

- `engine_core` must not depend on other internal crates (lowest layer).
- `script_editor` and `game_player` must not depend on each other.
- Circular dependencies are prohibited.

## Public API Design

- Re-export public modules from each crate root (`lib.rs`).
- Hide internal implementation with `pub(crate)`.
- Gate optional functionality with feature flags.

```rust
// engine_core/src/lib.rs
pub mod ecs;
pub mod renderer;
pub mod audio;
pub mod asset;
pub mod script;
pub mod scene;
pub mod save;

// internal only
pub(crate) mod ffi;
pub(crate) mod util;
```

## When Adding a New Crate

1. Create `crates/<name>/` directory.
2. `cargo init --lib crates/<name>`
3. Add it to `members` in root `Cargo.toml`.
4. Verify dependency-direction rules are not violated.
5. Add crate description to README.

See `.agent/workflows/new_crate.md` for detailed steps.
